  "id": "eval.2026-09-08-reflow-152600.agent-session-orchestration",
  "title": "Long-lived agent session orchestration",
  "description": "# Long-lived agent session orchestration\nRead left to right from client admission and scheduler placement into the runner's model/tool turn loop. Live output continues across disconnects; the durable event log supports replay from the client's last ACK and audit/metering.\n\nCompleted turns write immutable, content-addressed snapshot chains containing conversation, tool results and workspace files. Notes describe deduplication, fork reachability and collection. Lifecycle paths show safe checkpoint/release and heartbeat-triggered restoration, potentially on another host, before execution continues. Recovery repeats at most the in-flight turn, with idempotency keys protecting external writes.\n\nThe lower panel expands parent/child orchestration: scoped budgets and returned results, aggregate tree/workspace allowances, pause for user decisions, and orphan reaping. Notes cover cancellation propagation, held-child accounting and old-version deployment draining.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
